; expect 42
; `_` HOLES. An application with at least one bare `_` among its
; direct arguments desugars to a lambda, one fresh parameter per hole
; in left-to-right order: `(sub 50 _)` is `(lambda (y) (sub 50 y))`
; and `(sub _ 50)` is `(lambda (x) (sub x 50))`. No hole - an ordinary
; call - is untouched, so AX3013 (partial application of a top-level
; function with 0 holes and too few arguments) still fires exactly as
; before; see `tests/selfhost/` has no fixture for that because it is
; a diagnostic, pinned instead in the AXDL goldens.
;
; COLLISION CHECK, run before this was implemented: `_` was already
; meaningful as a WILDCARD PATTERN - a lambda/fn parameter, a match
; arm, a macro rule - and still is (`fstOf` below still discards its
; second field with a pattern `_`, unaffected). What changed is
; EXPRESSION position only, where a bare `_` used to resolve nowhere:
; `check` on `(add 5 _)` before this pass existed reported `E AX3001
; ... undefined variable \`_\`` with a "did you mean \`+\`" suggestion,
; because nothing - no binding, no function, no constructor, no
; builtin - is named `_`. Expression position had no existing meaning
; for a hole to collide with.
(:: sub (-> Int Int Int))
(fn (sub x y) (- x y))

(:: mul3 (-> Int Int Int Int))
(fn (mul3 x y z) (* x (* y z)))

(data Pair (a b) (Pair a b))

(:: fstOf (-> (Pair Int Int) Int))
(fn (fstOf p) (match p ((Pair x _) x)))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (let (
    (subFrom50 (sub 50 _))    ; (lambda (y) (sub 50 y))
    (subTo50 (sub _ 50))      ; (lambda (x) (sub x 50))
    (twoHoles (mul3 1 _ _))   ; (lambda (h0 h1) (mul3 1 h0 h1)), left to right
  )
    (+
      (subFrom50 8)                    ; 42
      (+
        (- (subTo50 100) 50)           ; 0
        (+
          (- (twoHoles 6 7) 42)        ; 0
          (fstOf (Pair 0 0))           ; 0
        )
      )
    )
  )
)
